# Review of SREDDY Database ORM and API choices :  New vs. OLD ; how they changed over time


## OLD way DB ORM and API design
### the old way
- Sreddy used to be big fan of TRpc and Zustand State Store in "Database API design layer"
- I guess the main reason for the above was 'type safety' when desiging 'front-end' ReactJS UI screens code
### what it costed
 - complex flow of TRPC server to client and mental overhead remembering and designing those flows
 - combined that complexity with 'NextJS'  client/server components designation in ReactJS pages is additional complexity/headache cognitive load
 - I guess 'Zustand store' may be independent layer , but still one more layer ..
 - and ReactQuery is another layer ...

## NEW way DB ORM and API design
### the new way
 - simple Drizzle schema.js table addition and let it create neeed DB API code
 - having Vite instead of NextJS removed so many other heaches .
### What it helped
 - simple design, easy to grok the concept in the head
 - know what is going on at any time ...